  "result": "Done! Added complete credit note functionality for processing refunds:\n\n**New module - src/credits.js:**\n\n`createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` creates credit notes (refunds) for issued invoices.\n\n**Features:**\n\n1. **Eligibility:**\n   - Works on invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n   - Rejects draft invoices with NOT_ISSUED error\n\n2. **Credit note number:**\n   - Format: CN-<year>-<counter> (e.g., CN-2025-0001, CN-2025-0002)\n   - Separate counter from invoices (both tracked in existingNumbers)\n   - Counter resets each year\n\n3. **Return format:**\n   ```javascript\n   {\n     number: 'CN-2025-0001',\n     invoiceNumber: 'INV-2025-0001',\n     customerId: 'C-001',\n     amount: 50000,              // in cents\n     reason: 'Partial refund',\n     date: '2025-10-20'\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. **Validation:**\n   - **NOT_ISSUED**: Draft invoices cannot have credit notes\n   - **AMOUNT_INVALID**: Amount must be positive integer (in cents)\n   - **CREDIT_TOO_HIGH**: Credit amount cannot exceed invoice total\n\n**Helper function:**\n- `nextCreditNoteNumber(existingNumbers, date)` - generates next CN number with independent counter\n\n**Tests added:** 14 tests covering:\n- Number generation and counter increment\n- Separate CN numbering from invoices\n- All invoice statuses (issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- Draft invoice rejection\n- Amount validation (zero, negative, fractional)\n- Credit amount vs invoice total validation\n- Edge case: credit equal to invoice total\n\n**Test results:** \u2705 All 189 tests pass (175 existing + 14 new)",
